      ],
      "op": "UNFLATTEN_FROM_STRING",
      "verified": true,
      "note": "Confirmed via NI doc (parses binary_string into type's type; error_in/out, byte_order 0/1/2=big/native/little default 0, includes_size default True, rest_of_string = leftover bytes) and via ~15 real corpus instances (dictionary/appcontrol/msgqueue/lvdata, plus JKI-VI-Tester) whose 'type'/'value' terminals (idx 7/2) vary together across Array/Cluster/Refnum/6 numeric types while 'error in'/'error out' (idx 8/0) stay fixed as the error cluster -- confirms the role split, not shape. Emitted via UNFLATTEN_FROM_STRING op handler (mirrors TYPE_CAST's dest-type-from-output-terminal reading), which defers to _lv.unflatten_from_string. Numeric-scalar/array<->string supported (length-prefixed when includes_size, all 3 byte orders); cluster/refnum/float targets (observed in this same corpus, e.g. Strip Units__ogtk.vi) raise loudly pending fuller flat-format support, same policy as Type Cast (1166)."
    },
